    "answer_text": "Biodegradable substances affect the environment in the following ways: (i) The biodegradable substances such as tree leaves, plant parts, and kitchen wastes can be used as humus after composting. This will enhance the soil fertility. (ii) The biodegradable substances mainly contain carbon. These substances after decomposition release that carbon back into the atmosphere.",
